--   **The size loop.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL3Top4`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL3H.zloopQ {c : IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL3H.Cfg} (hc : CfgOK c) {jZ : Fin Pp} {cont : IStmt HS Pp}
--       (hj : tbl jZ = zloopC c jZ cont) {P K D S ρ r w Mb Bz : ℕ} (hP : 1 ≤ P)
--       (hS : 1 ≤ S) (hr : 1 ≤ r) (hMb : zsz (Mb : ℤ) ≤ Bz)
--       (hM : 2 * aV c P S r w D + c.Aw * (D + 1) ^ c.p + (D + 1) ^ c.p + 2 * c.m + 10 ≤ Mb)
--       {f g : Fin HS → List ℤ} (hf : Clean0 f) (hg : Clean0 g) {cc : ℕ}
--       (Cont : ∀ σ, DescR σ P K D S ρ r w → σ 11 = some (Nat.size (aV c P S r w D) : ℤ) →
--         RunQ Isym tbl σ cont f g cc) :
--       ∀ n σ, (DescR σ P K D S ρ r w ∧ ∃ j : ℕ, σ 11 = some (j : ℤ) ∧
--         σ 12 = some ((2 ^ j : ℕ) : ℤ) ∧ j + n = Nat.size (aV c P S r w D)) →
--         RunQ Isym tbl σ (.call jZ) f g (cc + (n + 1) * cLoopS (szZ c) 2 Bz)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language (I3): the local size loop of the uniform Proposition 14
--
--   `zloopC c jZ cont`: with the descriptor registers, finds `j = Nat.size a` on `11` (`2^j` on `12`;
--   `zloopQ`), where `a = 32 W' P S r + w + EwH D`.  The local size bound is then `Zl = j + K D`, so
--   `zsz (32 W' P 2^{K D} S r) ≤ Zl` and `H + 1 < 2^{Zl}` for `H = w + EwH D` (`zl_spec`).  The field
--   width `G` is computed from `Zl` (not from the caller's `Z`), so the per-row factor is
--   `≈ log` of the size of the array and of the width bound.
